WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.934
-Come on!
-It is so good to see you.

00:00:02.934 --> 00:00:05.300
They love you. We love you.
Jon Hamm is in the house.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.100
-I feel the love.
-You feel it, right?

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.167
-I feel the love.
-You have to feel the love.

00:00:09.167 --> 00:00:10.267
-I very much do.

00:00:10.267 --> 00:00:11.734
-I have so much
to talk to you about.

00:00:11.734 --> 00:00:14.567
I know --
The St. Louis Blues, okay?

00:00:14.567 --> 00:00:17.167
You're a St. Louis sports fan.
-Game 5 tonight -- exciting.

00:00:17.167 --> 00:00:19.334
Exciting stuff.
We'll see what happens.

00:00:19.334 --> 00:00:22.334
-But I have to talk to you about
their game a few weeks ago.

00:00:22.334 --> 00:00:24.534
They were down 2-0, right?

00:00:24.534 --> 00:00:26.534
-Yeah, yeah. It happens.

00:00:26.534 --> 00:00:28.601
-Yeah. And you entered
the broadcast booth.

00:00:28.601 --> 00:00:31.267
-I came up to see some
friends in the broadcast booth,

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:32.701
John Kelly and Darren Pang.

00:00:32.701 --> 00:00:35.767
They invited me up to come
switch a little mojo around.

00:00:35.767 --> 00:00:38.934
-Yeah. They're down 2-zip, okay?

00:00:38.934 --> 00:00:40.400
Let's take a look at
what happened.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:43.267
-The shot. And they score!

00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:44.701
Jon Hamm is in our booth,

00:00:44.701 --> 00:00:49.367
and just like that, his boy,
Barbashev, sets up the goal.

00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:52.133
And it's in! My goodness!

00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:55.901
The magic of Jon Hamm
in the booth strikes again.

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:58.234
And he just scored!
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.234 --> 00:01:00.467
You have done it again!

00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:02.467
-You can't write this.

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:05.067
-And another goal by
Perron and the Blues!

00:01:05.067 --> 00:01:06.734
-I literally can't leave
at this point.

00:01:06.734 --> 00:01:07.901
-You can't.

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:11.968
-They scored four goals!
-Four!

00:01:11.968 --> 00:01:14.100
-In six minutes.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.534
Four goals in six minutes,
which is unheard of.

00:01:16.534 --> 00:01:17.601
-That was crazy.

00:01:17.601 --> 00:01:19.367
Yeah, it was a very --
It was so weird.

00:01:19.367 --> 00:01:21.834
Like, you couldn't write that.
It was just crazy.

00:01:21.834 --> 00:01:24.834
-Was it -- Every name you
were saying, they were --

00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:26.567
-That person would then score.

00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:29.067
It was like -- It was
the weirdest experience

00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:30.167
I've ever had in a hockey rink.

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:31.300
-Ever, right?
-Yeah.

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:33.367
-Well, now the Blues
are in the playoffs.

00:01:33.367 --> 00:01:34.667
They want you for every game?

00:01:34.667 --> 00:01:36.567
-Yeah. There's a game tonight.

00:01:36.567 --> 00:01:38.901
I actually have to leave here,
and fly right --

00:01:38.901 --> 00:01:40.133
I fly right to the booth.

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:41.634
-Yeah. Congrats on that.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:42.968
That was just such a cool --
-That was very fun.

00:01:42.968 --> 00:01:45.167
-Only in Jon Hamm's world.
That's so cool.

00:01:45.167 --> 00:01:47.400
But you were in the --
You were just in one of

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:49.067
the coolest things a
human could do.

00:01:49.067 --> 00:01:52.334
You were in George Harrison's
video for "My Sweet Lord."

00:01:52.334 --> 00:01:54.033
-That was very cool, yes.

00:01:54.033 --> 00:01:55.434
-How did you get
involved with that?

00:01:55.434 --> 00:01:57.868
-Lance Bangs, who's a really
wonderful director --

00:01:57.868 --> 00:01:59.667
He's directed "Jackass"
and a bunch of music videos

00:01:59.667 --> 00:02:00.834
here and there.

00:02:00.834 --> 00:02:04.067
Kind of one of those guys
had asked me --

00:02:04.067 --> 00:02:06.801
told me that Dhani Harrison,
George's son,

00:02:06.801 --> 00:02:08.934
was a fan of mine,
and would I be interested in

00:02:08.934 --> 00:02:10.968
being in the music video
they're making for

00:02:10.968 --> 00:02:13.133
the 50th anniversary
of the release of that song?

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:15.567
And I was like,
"Well, just so happens

00:02:15.567 --> 00:02:17.534
George Harrison's
my favorite Beatle,

00:02:17.534 --> 00:02:20.534
and 'My Sweet Lord' is one of my
favorite songs of all time."

00:02:20.534 --> 00:02:21.534
And I was like,
"Yes, absolutely.

00:02:21.534 --> 00:02:22.534
I'd love to do that."

00:02:22.534 --> 00:02:24.934
And I, you know,
shot it on my phone.

00:02:24.934 --> 00:02:26.934
It was during, like, lockdown
and COVID and everything,

00:02:26.934 --> 00:02:28.868
so we all kind of
had to do it ourselves,

00:02:28.868 --> 00:02:30.334
but it was -- It was amazing.

00:02:30.334 --> 00:02:31.834
-I mean, I don't know.

00:02:31.834 --> 00:02:32.901
I know you're a big Beatles fan,

00:02:32.901 --> 00:02:34.334
but now you're in
the official music video.

00:02:34.334 --> 00:02:35.434
-I know. It's crazy.
-Yeah.

00:02:35.434 --> 00:02:36.968
-It's crazy.

00:02:36.968 --> 00:02:38.734
-Is there a rumor that
I heard that Paul McCartney

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:40.667
was going to be in "Mad Men"?

00:02:40.667 --> 00:02:42.801
Did I make that up?

00:02:42.801 --> 00:02:44.100
-It would have been hard to have

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:45.667
the actual Paul McCartney
in "Mad Men,"

00:02:45.667 --> 00:02:48.133
'cause the real Paul McCartney
was like 26 years old

00:02:48.133 --> 00:02:50.901
during "Mad Men,"
so it would have been an odd --

00:02:50.901 --> 00:02:53.467
-[ As McCartney ] Well,
I wouldn't be playing meself.

00:02:53.467 --> 00:02:55.000
-[ As McCartney ] I'd have to
play some sort of

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.501
advertising genius.

00:02:56.501 --> 00:02:58.968
-A genius. I know.
-Something like that.

00:02:58.968 --> 00:03:02.033
What are you doing, Don Draper?"

00:03:02.033 --> 00:03:03.834
More, man.
-Don Draper, put it on record.

00:03:03.834 --> 00:03:07.234
-Let your mind go.

00:03:07.234 --> 00:03:10.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:10.033 --> 00:03:11.067
-[ Normal voice ] Come on!

00:03:11.067 --> 00:03:12.934
That would've been great!

00:03:12.934 --> 00:03:14.534
Is there any truth
to that story or not?

00:03:14.534 --> 00:03:15.601
-Not that I know of.
-Not that you know of.

00:03:15.601 --> 00:03:17.400
-I mean, maybe
he was considering it.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:19.167
And certainly not
after that impression.

00:03:19.167 --> 00:03:21.267
-No, no, no. Of course not.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:22.701
Let's talk about
"Top Gun: Maverick."

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:24.968
-Let's!
-Last time you were here --

00:03:24.968 --> 00:03:26.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:26.734 --> 00:03:28.834
Last time you were here,
you described it as

00:03:28.834 --> 00:03:30.234
"the movie
version of a high five."

00:03:30.234 --> 00:03:31.734
-Yeah, a visual high five.
-Yeah.

00:03:31.734 --> 00:03:33.367
-It really is.
-And it --

00:03:33.367 --> 00:03:35.734
-In fact, we might break the
record this weekend

00:03:35.734 --> 00:03:38.300
for most high fives
in a weekend.

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:39.367
-We had a screening,

00:03:39.367 --> 00:03:40.801
we went to it here,

00:03:40.801 --> 00:03:45.167
and everyone was screaming,
standing up, crying, laughing.

00:03:45.167 --> 00:03:50.601
It's just a giant, awesome
summer movie that you want.

00:03:50.601 --> 00:03:53.334
It's a popcorn movie.
It is a family movie.

00:03:53.334 --> 00:03:56.434
It is friends movie.
It is everything you could want.

00:03:56.434 --> 00:03:58.801
And you miss going to theaters.
-That's it.

00:03:58.801 --> 00:04:01.234
It's a welcome back
to the movies.

00:04:01.234 --> 00:04:02.968
You know, and it's, like,
you get to see it --

00:04:02.968 --> 00:04:04.868
It's only released in theaters.

00:04:04.868 --> 00:04:06.467
It's not on
a streaming platform.

00:04:06.467 --> 00:04:10.033
You can't watch it
on your phone -- legally.

00:04:10.033 --> 00:04:12.334
-Of course not.
Yeah, no one brought --

00:04:12.334 --> 00:04:14.567
-You know, it's in Dolby and 4K
and all of the stuff.

00:04:14.567 --> 00:04:16.167
-The sound is intense.

00:04:16.167 --> 00:04:19.534
The seats vibrate
when the jets take off.

00:04:19.534 --> 00:04:23.167
And you know what it is, too?
-You pay for a whole seat.

00:04:23.167 --> 00:04:24.400
-Yes, that's true.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:25.701
-But you're only going to use
the edge of it.

00:04:25.701 --> 00:04:27.767
-Oh!

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:30.100
Whew!

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:32.100
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:37.634 --> 00:04:40.534
Oh, someone picks up that line
and puts that somewhere,

00:04:40.534 --> 00:04:42.467
that'll be the best thing that
ever happened to you.

00:04:42.467 --> 00:04:44.000
-Well...

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.000
-But you know what
I was going to say,

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:49.234
is how much respect
you have for our

00:04:49.234 --> 00:04:50.300
service-men and -women.

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:51.334
-It was impressive.

00:04:51.334 --> 00:04:53.100
Getting the chance to
make this movie,

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:55.367
we shot the majority of it in

00:04:55.367 --> 00:04:57.334
North Island Naval Base
in San Diego, California,

00:04:57.334 --> 00:05:00.434
Coronado Island,
and we shot a lot of it on

00:05:00.434 --> 00:05:05.133
the USS Theodore Roosevelt,
"America's Big Stick,"

00:05:05.133 --> 00:05:07.300
which is a
working aircraft carrier,

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:10.033
which is 10 stories high
and about a city block long.

00:05:10.033 --> 00:05:13.667
5,500 sailors on it, 75 to 80
aircraft at any one time,

00:05:13.667 --> 00:05:15.901
two working nuclear reactors.

00:05:15.901 --> 00:05:18.367
And to see the -- I asked
the guy --

00:05:18.367 --> 00:05:21.100
the captain of the ship --
I said, "What's the range?"

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:23.033
He goes, "We can go forever."
-Yeah.

00:05:23.033 --> 00:05:25.267
-And I was like, "Oh, okay."

00:05:25.267 --> 00:05:26.534
-You're like,
"I'm an actor," yeah.

00:05:26.534 --> 00:05:27.767
-"Good to know," yeah.

00:05:27.767 --> 00:05:30.434
"Where's the off,
and how do I not touch anything

00:05:30.434 --> 00:05:31.434
that's going to explode?"

00:05:31.434 --> 00:05:32.701
-Yeah.

00:05:32.701 --> 00:05:34.534
-But it is impressive to see
the sacrifices that

00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:36.634
the service-men and -women
go through every day,

00:05:36.634 --> 00:05:37.734
and just to keep us safe.

00:05:37.734 --> 00:05:39.267
It's an impressive thing,

00:05:39.267 --> 00:05:41.100
and the movie is very much a
love letter to that, too.

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:44.534
-Yeah, so thankful to everyone
out there in our armed forces.

00:05:44.534 --> 00:05:45.701
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Fleet Week. It's Fleet Week.

00:05:45.701 --> 00:05:48.100
-And it's Fleet Week
here in New York.

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:50.734
I know you did press
everywhere for this movie.

00:05:50.734 --> 00:05:52.601
It's a giant movie.
It's a global --

00:05:52.601 --> 00:05:54.067
-Global.
-It's a global movie.

00:05:54.067 --> 00:05:56.133
Everyone everywhere
is watching it this weekend.

00:05:56.133 --> 00:05:58.667
You went and you met the royals.

00:05:58.667 --> 00:06:01.334
-Some royals.
-And have you ever met --

00:06:01.334 --> 00:06:02.801
-Not the Kansas City Royals.

00:06:02.801 --> 00:06:04.200
-No, this is --
-A very different kind.

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:07.234
-You actually went to England.
-England. London, England.

00:06:07.234 --> 00:06:10.601
We met Kate and William, the
Duke and Duchess of Cambridge.

00:06:10.601 --> 00:06:11.968
-Yes.

00:06:11.968 --> 00:06:16.100
-There are some guidelines
that are not so much guidelines,

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:18.567
but hard-and-fast rules
that you are made to follow

00:06:18.567 --> 00:06:20.234
when you meet the royalty.

00:06:20.234 --> 00:06:23.534
-Like you bow.
-There's a bow involved.

00:06:23.534 --> 00:06:25.734
If you're a lady,
you may bow or curtsy.

00:06:25.734 --> 00:06:28.801
-Yep. I'm sure Tom Cruise
knows how to do all this.

00:06:28.801 --> 00:06:30.901
-Tom's, like, got it all
on lock, of course.

00:06:30.901 --> 00:06:32.000
-He's like,
"Yeah, I've done this.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:34.100
Yeah, I've met
the queen before, yeah.

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:35.567
Let me text her before we go."

00:06:35.567 --> 00:06:37.234
It's like, "I'm coming over."
Yeah, yeah, exactly.

00:06:37.234 --> 00:06:39.701
-"HMH. How you doin'?

00:06:39.701 --> 00:06:42.167
Elizabeth Regina Deuce."

00:06:44.033 --> 00:06:45.701
But it was
a very cool experience.

00:06:45.701 --> 00:06:47.968
They couldn't be nicer.

00:06:47.968 --> 00:06:49.534
Prince William had --

00:06:49.534 --> 00:06:51.868
It was black tie,
so we're all in tuxedos.

00:06:51.868 --> 00:06:58.267
And Prince William had on his
tuxedo shoes, embroidered F-18s.

00:06:58.267 --> 00:06:59.300
-Wow!

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:01.334
-Very cool
"Top Gun" tuxedo shoes.

00:07:01.334 --> 00:07:04.534
-That's very cool.
-That means you've made it.

00:07:04.534 --> 00:07:06.300
So I no longer
worry about the prince.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:07.434
I feel like he's made it.
He's got it.

00:07:07.434 --> 00:07:08.968
-Yeah, he's made it, yeah.

00:07:08.968 --> 00:07:10.467
Did everyone follow
the directions?

00:07:10.467 --> 00:07:11.567
-Pretty much.

00:07:11.567 --> 00:07:13.400
I mean, I think there
might have been

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:14.534
a few breaches of etiquette.

00:07:14.534 --> 00:07:16.167
Did you have something in mind?

00:07:16.167 --> 00:07:18.934
-I heard a story that
maybe Miles Teller

00:07:18.934 --> 00:07:20.968
was kind of freaking out,
because --

00:07:20.968 --> 00:07:23.934
-He geeked out a little
on Prince William's eyes.

00:07:23.934 --> 00:07:25.300
I remember coming back
afterwards.

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:26.567
He was like, "They're so blue.

00:07:26.567 --> 00:07:29.968
I got lost in his eyes."

00:07:29.968 --> 00:07:32.000
I was like, "Okay.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:33.234
I didn't think we were allowed
to look at him in the eye,

00:07:33.234 --> 00:07:34.701
but alright."

00:07:34.701 --> 00:07:37.133
-You just bow and you move on.
-You bow and you move on, man.

00:07:37.133 --> 00:07:39.200
-But he told him
that he loved his eyes?

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:40.868
-Yeah.
I was like, "You told the guy

00:07:40.868 --> 00:07:42.901
you feel in love,
like, you got lost in his eyes?"

00:07:42.901 --> 00:07:45.767
He goes, "I think. I don't know.
I've lost my mind."

00:07:45.767 --> 00:07:48.868
-I heard this story,
and then we found the photo.

00:07:48.868 --> 00:07:50.634
And I'm not kidding,
I think this is the moment that

00:07:50.634 --> 00:07:53.367
Miles Teller got lost in
Prince William's eyes.

00:07:53.367 --> 00:07:54.400
Take a look at this.

00:07:57.934 --> 00:07:59.968
I'm getting lost in his eyes,
as well.

00:07:59.968 --> 00:08:02.834
-So's Jen Connelly, too.
Everybody.

00:08:02.834 --> 00:08:04.334
-Everyone's into his eyes.
-Everyone wants a piece.

00:08:04.334 --> 00:08:06.667
-Oh, gosh, she was great in
the movie, as well.

00:08:06.667 --> 00:08:09.133
Can you tell everyone
who you play in the film?

00:08:09.133 --> 00:08:10.634
-I play kind of the boss.

00:08:10.634 --> 00:08:12.634
In fact, my official title is

00:08:12.634 --> 00:08:16.033
Vice Admiral
Beau "Cyclone" Simpson.

00:08:16.033 --> 00:08:18.200
-Cyclone.
-Cyclone is my call sign.

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:22.067
Former Top Gun graduate, current
air boss of the Pacific Fleet.

00:08:22.067 --> 00:08:25.901
And so I kind of run all of
the aircraft on the big carrier

00:08:25.901 --> 00:08:27.734
when the big mission comes down.

00:08:27.734 --> 00:08:29.634
And I have to set some
rules and regulations, Jimmy,

00:08:29.634 --> 00:08:31.968
and I don't like people
that break rules.

00:08:31.968 --> 00:08:32.968
-That's right.

00:08:32.968 --> 00:08:34.601
-So when I run up against a guy

00:08:34.601 --> 00:08:36.868
whose name
is literally Maverick...

00:08:36.868 --> 00:08:38.701
-Wow.
He's gonna get the Cyclone.

00:08:38.701 --> 00:08:40.501
-...a little of this.
-He's gonna get the Cyclone.

00:08:40.501 --> 00:08:41.634
-A little buttin' heads.

00:08:41.634 --> 00:08:43.234
He's gonna have to
answer to Cyclone.

00:08:43.234 --> 00:08:44.901
-Yeah. Get ready
for everyone to be, like,

00:08:44.901 --> 00:08:45.934
yelling at you, "Cyclone!"

00:08:45.934 --> 00:08:47.734
-"Cyclone, baby!"
-I mean, come on.

00:08:47.734 --> 00:08:49.000
You were so good in this, bud.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:51.400
-The really cool thing about
my call sign is that

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:53.234
I actually have an emoji.

00:08:53.234 --> 00:08:55.000
There's an emoji
that's a little tornado,

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:57.200
so I can now sign off
with an emoji.

00:08:57.200 --> 00:09:00.501
-Yeah!
That's what I'm talking about.

00:09:00.501 --> 00:09:03.901
You told me it was good.
It came out. It is beyond good.

00:09:03.901 --> 00:09:06.634
You were very humble.
You didn't oversell it at all.

00:09:06.634 --> 00:09:07.968
You were fantastic.
-I'm so glad you liked it.

00:09:07.968 --> 00:09:09.834
-The movie is great.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:09:09.834 --> 00:09:12.701
Here's Jon Hamm and Tom Cruise
in "Top Gun: Maverick."

00:09:12.701 --> 00:09:13.801
Take a look at this.

00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:19.767
-Captain Pete
"Maverick" Mitchell.

00:09:19.767 --> 00:09:21.701
Your reputation precedes you.

00:09:21.701 --> 00:09:24.033
-Thank you, sir.

00:09:24.033 --> 00:09:26.701
-Wasn't a compliment.

00:09:28.501 --> 00:09:29.601
I'm Admiral Beau Simpson.

00:09:29.601 --> 00:09:30.701
I'm the air boss.

00:09:30.701 --> 00:09:31.868
I believe you know
Admiral Bates.

00:09:31.868 --> 00:09:33.534
-Warlock, sir.

00:09:33.534 --> 00:09:36.267
I must admit, I wasn't expecting
an invitation back.

00:09:36.267 --> 00:09:38.234
-They're called orders,
Maverick.

00:09:38.234 --> 00:09:40.934
You two have
something in common.

00:09:40.934 --> 00:09:43.834
Cyclone here was
first in his class back in '88.

00:09:43.834 --> 00:09:46.467
-Actually, sir,
I finished second.

00:09:46.467 --> 00:09:48.701
Just want to
manage the expectations.

00:09:48.701 --> 00:09:50.767
-Yeah, exactly right. Come on.

00:09:50.767 --> 00:09:52.033
That's Jon Hamm, everybody.

00:09:52.033 --> 00:09:55.400
"Top Gun: Maverick"
hits theaters, Dolby Cinema,

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:57.100
and IMAX this Friday.

00:09:57.100 --> 00:09:58.133
Go see it in IMAX.

